    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "rpc: reject setban bantime that would overflow",
    "user": {
      "login": "Bruce039",
      "id": 109469941,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBoZg9Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109469941?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bruce039",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`BanMan::Ban` computes the ban end as `GetTime() + bantime` (banman.cpp:140). `setban` takes `bantime` as any int64, so a relative bantime close to `INT64_MAX`:\n\n```\nsetban 1.2.3.5 add 9223372036854775807\n```\n\nreturns success, but the sum overflows. UBSan reports:\n\n```\nsrc/banman.cpp:140:73: runtime error: signed integer overflow: 1790412558 + 9223372036854775807 cannot be represented in type 'int64_t'\n```\n\nWithout UBSan the result wraps negative, the ban is treated as already expired, and `listbanned` stays empty.\n\nThis makes `setban` reject a relative bantime that doesn't fit when added to the current time, with \"Error: bantime is too large\" (RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER), next to the existing check for absolute timestamps in the past. The ban logic itself is unchanged. `-bantime` isn't touched here: startup args generally aren't range checked.\n\nThe added case in `rpc_setban.py` checks that `setban` with a bantime of `INT64_MAX` is rejected and nothing gets banned. It fails on master (\"No exception raised\") and passes with the change. `p2p_disconnect_ban.py` still passes.\n\nAI tools were used to help find this issue and to prepare the patch and test.\n",
