      "body": "I am not sure about starting/trying to support durations that C++ itself doesn't even support (https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/chrono/duration) \r\n\r\nI think it would be fine to reject args that are too large. Though, argparsing doesn't really do any verification and I am sure you can find an int overflow for basically every single arg. Also, `SaturatingAdd` doesn't work for chrono types ...",
