        }
      ],
      "message": "rpc: reject setban bantime that would overflow\n\nBanMan::Ban computes the ban end as GetTime() + bantime. The setban RPC\ntakes bantime as any int64, so a relative bantime close to INT64_MAX\noverflows there (UBSan: signed integer overflow in banman.cpp). In\npractice the result wraps negative, the ban is treated as expired, and\nit is silently dropped even though the RPC returns success.\n\nReject relative bantimes that don't fit when added to the current time,\nlike absolute timestamps in the past are already rejected.",
